@startuml thread_overview
title Zephyr Threads & Synchronisation Primitives

skinparam defaultFontSize 12

rectangle "K_THREAD_DEFINE\ncontrol_loop_thread\n(stack 1024, prio APPLICATION)" as t_cl
rectangle "K_THREAD_DEFINE\nmotion_control_events_thread\n(stack 1024, prio APPLICATION)" as t_mc
rectangle "k_thread_create\nmqtt_pubsub_thread\n(stack 4096, prio 7)" as t_mqtt

database "K_SEM\nset_point_sem\n(initial=1, limit=1)" as sem
queue "K_MSGQ\nmotion_control_events_queue\n(depth=MOTION_CONTROL_EVENT_MAX)" as msgq

t_cl --> sem : k_sem_take / k_sem_give\n(protect trajectory update)
t_mc --> msgq : k_msgq_put (event_post)\nk_msgq_get (dispatch)
t_cl <-- t_mc : calls control_loop_set_target_setpoint()\n  which takes set_point_sem
t_mqtt --> t_mc : calls motion_control_event_post()\n  → k_msgq_put (non-blocking K_NO_WAIT)

note bottom of t_mqtt
  SYS_INIT(mqtt_pubsub_init, APPLICATION, ...)
  creates the thread at boot
end note

note bottom of t_mc
  Blocks on k_msgq_get(K_FOREVER)
  Dispatches to rx/tx handler arrays
end note

note bottom of t_cl
  Busy loop (no sleep).
  Inner sim runs 1000×1µs per
  1ms control tick.
end note

@enduml
